1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,437
Two Tickets, Please.

3
00:00:03,437 --> 00:00:06,510
Dad and I arrive at the movie theater twenty minutes early.

4
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:09,615
I have one job today: help choose the seats.

5
00:00:09,615 --> 00:00:12,719
Dad says this is more important than choosing the popcorn.

6
00:00:12,719 --> 00:00:14,958
I am not completely convinced.

7
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:16,412
Hi there.

8
00:00:16,412 --> 00:00:18,120
What would you like to see?

9
00:00:18,388 --> 00:00:20,653
The animated movie at two thirty.

10
00:00:20,653 --> 00:00:22,590
Two tickets, please.

11
00:00:22,876 --> 00:00:24,005
Sure.

12
00:00:24,005 --> 00:00:25,807
Here's the seating chart.

13
00:00:25,807 --> 00:00:29,016
The gray seats are taken, and the blue ones are available.

14
00:00:29,284 --> 00:00:31,067
Are there seats near the middle?

15
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:33,252
Row six has two together.

16
00:00:33,252 --> 00:00:35,981
Or you can sit closer to the front in row three.

17
00:00:36,268 --> 00:00:38,355
Row six sounds good to me.

18
00:00:38,355 --> 00:00:39,845
What do you think?

19
00:00:40,132 --> 00:00:41,334
Perfect.

20
00:00:41,334 --> 00:00:44,042
I don't want to spend the whole movie looking straight up.

21
00:00:44,042 --> 00:00:46,636
We get our tickets and move away from the counter.

22
00:00:46,636 --> 00:00:49,261
Then I realize I forgot to ask one thing.

23
00:00:49,261 --> 00:00:51,199
Which way is theater three?

24
00:00:51,484 --> 00:00:54,600
Down the hall on your left, just past the restrooms.

25
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:56,001
Thanks.

26
00:00:56,001 --> 00:00:58,470
We find our seats with plenty of time.

27
00:00:58,470 --> 00:01:01,241
I check the numbers twice before we sit down.

28
00:01:01,516 --> 00:01:03,093
Excellent planning.

29
00:01:03,093 --> 00:01:05,228
Now, about that popcorn.

30
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,254
I knew it was important.

31
00:01:07,254 --> 00:01:10,723
We share a small bag and watch the screen fill with trailers.

32
00:01:10,723 --> 00:01:14,900
Before the movie starts, Dad silences his phone, and I do the same.

33
00:01:15,172 --> 00:01:17,028
Ready for the adventure?

34
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:18,420
Yes.

35
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:21,618
Middle seats, snacks, and no neck pain.

36
00:01:21,618 --> 00:01:25,129
I think my first day as the family seat expert is going pretty well.
